      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the silence stretches out like that, it becomes a suffocating weight, and the desire for it to simply end is a deeply understandable response to prolonged pain. If the grey is all you see, perhaps finding a single, sharp point of color—even a tiny, intense feeling—might be a worthwhile thing to focus on. Reaching out to a professional can offer a structured way to navigate this overwhelming quietness and find a different kind of peace.",
